SUSPECTED BUG: origins wrapped in a concrete error value are lost when it is passed as a method receiver (or any concrete-typed parameter) and converted to error in the callee.
`return r.find(key).OrNil()`: OrNil returns its non-nil receiver, so Stat returns exactly find's non-nil values.
Expected: find's 3 entries (kverr.ErrEmptyKey, engine.ErrClosed, kverr.ErrNotFound), each under *kverr.OpError.Unwrap; no typed nil.
Actual: 1 bare `concrete *kverr.OpError` positioned inside OrNil: no chain, no Unresolved entry, so the set hides that errors.Is(err, kverr.ErrNotFound) can hold
(a later errors.Is guard on such a value is ignored without a 'possibly handled' note).
